mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "36644285"}, {"study_label": "PQQ glaucoma review (preclinical)", "outcome": "ATP content", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42653764"}, {"study_label": "PQQ glaucoma review (preclinical)", "outcome": "cell viability", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42653764"}, {"study_label": "PQQ glaucoma review (preclinical)", "outcome": "RGC density", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42653764"}, {"study_label": "PQQ glaucoma review (preclinical)", "outcome": "NAD+ levels along the visual pathway", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42653764"}, {"study_label": "PQQ glaucoma review (preclinical)", "outcome": "functional improvement (RCT, glaucoma patients)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42653764"}, {"study_label": "NR MTD integrative review (meta)", "outcome": "mitochondrial function / NAD+ homeostasis (integrative review synthesis)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "41516357"}], "gap_cells": [{"intervention": "nicotinamide riboside (NR)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 4, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42669151", "40846977", "41516357", "NCT07344636"]}, {"intervention": "niacin (NAD+ precursor)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["39173541"]}, {"intervention": "NAD+ precursors (NR/NMN)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42489969"]}, {"intervention": "Combined Metabolic Activators (NR/NMN)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["37271226"]}, {"intervention": "nicotinamide riboside (NR) + exercise", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT04907110"]}, {"intervention": "urolithin A (Mitopure)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT07517913"]}, {"intervention": "nicotinamide riboside (NR)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["36644285"]}, {"intervention": "stable-isotope-labeled NR (13C/15N-NR)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42122439"]}, {"intervention": "NAD+ precursors (NMN/NR)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42047243"]}, {"intervention": "urolithin A", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42616901", "42432192"]}, {"intervention": "mitophagy interventions (pharmacological, substrate-based, exercise)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42746169"]}, {"intervention": "gut-derived metabolites (NAD+/SIRT3-linked)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42609595"]}, {"intervention": "nicotinamide riboside chloride (NRC)", "disease": "alcohol-induced neuronal damage (neurodegeneration)", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42327979"]}, {"intervention": "natural bioactive compounds (dietary fibers, polyphenols)", "disease": "myocardial infarction", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["41927585"]}, {"intervention": "NAD supplementation (NR)", "disease": "acute myeloid leukaemia", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42514364"]}, {"intervention": "nicotinamide mononucleotide (NMN)", "disease": "sepsis-induced acute kidney injury", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42585475"]}, {"intervention": "urolithin A", "disease": "Parkinson's disease", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42570712"]}, {"intervention": "NAD+ precursors (NAD+ boosters)", "disease": "musculoskeletal diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42727834"]}, {"intervention": "urolithin A + urolithin B", "disease": "muscle health (skeletal muscle)", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42773997"]}, {"intervention": "Restorin NR (NR fumarate)", "disease": "aging", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42582917"]}, {"intervention": "nicotinamide riboside (NR)", "disease": "peripheral artery disease", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT07782671"]}, {"intervention": "urolithin A (Mitopure)", "disease": "frailty in older adults", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT06556706"]}, {"intervention": "urolithin A (Mitopure)", "disease": "not specified (bioavailability/PK)", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT07231848"]}, {"intervention": "pyrroloquinoline quinone (PQQ)", "disease": "glaucoma", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42653764"]}], "insights": ["No head-to-head comparison is possible from this evidence base: none of the 28 extracted records reports a standard-of-care comparator arm (GDMT for CHF, idebenone for LhON, supportive care for primary MTD), so every marker in the direction matrix is mito-only and the central clinical question (mito therapy vs standard treatment) remains unanswered (36644285, 39173541, 42432192).", "Chronic heart failure: the strongest patient-relevant signal is preclinical urolithin A - significant improvements in diastolic function and attenuation of remodeling (42616901) and non-significant alleviation of diastolic dysfunction, hypertrophy and fibrosis in HFpEF mice (42432192); the only human data is a single-arm NR Ph1 (observational, low confidence) that doubled whole-blood NAD+ and improved PBMC respiration (36644285); the 'meta'-tiered NAD+ precursor CHF record is a review stating trials are ongoing, not a pooled effect estimate (42047243).", "Primary mitochondrial diseases: human evidence is sparse and non-confirmatory - niacin in a single patient gave a meager response and did not stop disease progression (low confidence, n=1) (39173541); a one-day double-blind CMA (NR/NMN) study showed only biomarker NAD+ elevation without clinical endpoints (37271226); and in a preclinical MTD animal model NR aggravated erythrocyte maturation defects, worsening anemia - the clearest negative effect in the set (42669151).", "LhON: zero records in this set - despite idebenone being the standard of care, the mito-vs-idebenone comparison is completely empty; the nearest optic-nerve data (PQQ in glaucoma) is a different disease and a narrative review tiered preclinical per the record, even though the text cites a PQQ-combination RCT with functional improvement that cannot be tiered rct without the primary report (42653764).", "Pipeline, not proof: an NR phase 3 PAD trial (n=250; NCT07782671), an NR MTD Ph1 (NCT07344636), a planned NR+exercise MTD trial (NCT04907110), a Mitopure frailty pilot RCT (NCT06556706) and urolithin A PK/bioavailability studies (NCT07231848, NCT07517913) have no posted results and therefore count as pipeline activity only, not evidence of effect.", "Mixed or negative syntheses temper the field: a meta-analytic synthesis of gut-metabolite/NAD+-SIRT3 signaling in CHF was associated with myocardial fibrosis, oxidative stress, mitochondrial dysfunction and adverse outcomes (42609595); mitophagy in CHF is described as a context-dependent rather than uniformly protective regulator (42746169); and musculoskeletal NAD+ booster evidence is at unclear/promising-foundation level only (42727834)."]}